## Context

`Erg.HasLog` and `Erg.HasBody` are always equal to `LogSepCount > 0` and
`BodySepCount > 0` respectively. They are redundant fields. Deferred from
ticket 0093 (spec-as-code foundation) to keep that PR focused on constant
extraction.

## Actions

1. Remove `HasLog` and `HasBody` from the `Erg` struct in `ticket.go`.
2. In `validate.go` rule 11: replace `!t.HasLog` with `t.LogSepCount == 0`
   and `!t.HasBody` with `t.BodySepCount == 0`.
3. Update `ticket_test.go`: remove assertions on `HasLog`/`HasBody` fields.
4. Run `make test`.

## Exit criteria
- `Erg` struct has no `HasLog` or `HasBody` fields.
- `validate.go` uses `LogSepCount`/`BodySepCount` for rule 11.
- `make test` passes.
